# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# thuis: Adverb. "at home at one's dwelling or in one's home area"
# terug: Adverb. "backwards, back (in the opposite direction)"
# aan: Adverb. "on, (of a device) being operative"
# op: Adverb. "up"
# me: Pronoun. "form of unstressed form (me)"
# mij: Pronoun. "me; first-person singular objective personal pronoun"
# je: Pronoun. "inflection of jij (subjective, unstressed, form)"
# jou: Pronoun. "you; second-person singular objective personal pronoun"
# hem: Pronoun. "him; third-person singular masculine objective personal pronoun"
# haar: Pronoun. "her; third-person singular feminine objective personal pronoun"
# ons: Pronoun. "us; first-person plural objective personal pronoun"
# jullie: Pronoun. "you; second-person plural subjective personal pronoun"
# ze: Pronoun. "form of unstressed form (she) (feminine singular subject)"
thuis
terug
aan
op
me
mij
je
jou
hem
haar
ons
jullie
ze
